PKGSTATE-CHECK(1)

# NAME

pkgstate-check - validate and summarize native installed state

# SYNOPSIS

*pkgstate-check* *--canonical-store* _path_ \
               *--managed-target* _identity_ \
               *--state-store* _identity_ \
               *--root-view* _identity_ \
               *--state-backend* _identity_ \
               *--publication-domain* _identity_ \

*pkgstate-check* {*-V* | *-h*}

# DESCRIPTION

*pkgstate-check* opens an existing canonical generation store, validates its
binding and selected generation, and prints one complete report. The command is
read-only. It does not initialize a missing store, repair records, publish a
generation, execute lifecycle programs, or import another package database.

# OPTIONS

*-c*, *--canonical-store*=_path_
	Inspect the existing generation store at _path_.

*--managed-target*=_identity_
	Expected managed-target identity.

*--state-store*=_identity_
	Expected durable state-store identity.

*--root-view*=_identity_
	Expected logical target root-view identity.

*--state-backend*=_identity_
	Expected state-backend identity.

*--publication-domain*=_identity_
	Expected publication-domain identity.

*-V*, *--version*
	Print version and exit.

*-h*, *--help*
	Print usage and exit.

# OUTPUT

The report includes storage format, target binding, snapshot and ownership
identities, package and ownership counts, rejected-object references, and package
counts by installation reason.

# EXIT STATUS

0
	The store is valid and the report was emitted.

1
	The store or binding is invalid.

2
	Command-line usage is invalid.

# SEE ALSO

*pkgstate-generation*(5), *pkgstate_canonical_generation_store*(3)
